From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: defconfig: Enable the Allwinner sun8i PWM driver

The Allwinner A733 has PWM controllers that the pwm-sun8i driver
handles. Without CONFIG_PWM_SUN8I the defconfig kernel builds no driver
for them.

Build the driver as a module. No device needs it to boot, and the
controllers are disabled in the device tree until a board enables them.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on one board; the module loads and
binds to PWM1.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/configs/defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
index b80682c6b027..749326646d99 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
@@ -1745,6 +1745,7 @@ CONFIG_PWM_SAMSUNG=y
 CONFIG_PWM_SL28CPLD=m
 CONFIG_PWM_STM32=m
 CONFIG_PWM_SUN4I=m
+CONFIG_PWM_SUN8I=m
 CONFIG_PWM_TEGRA=m
 CONFIG_PWM_TIECAP=m
 CONFIG_PWM_TIEHRPWM=m
